From the diagram
CPU  1 fat control   1 mid cache   1 huge lower cache   9 ALUs
GPU  5 thin control+cache stacks   1 shared lower cache   20 ALUs

Types
CONTROL   instruction decode, schedule, branch, exception
ALU       integer / FP arithmetic and logic
CACHE     on-die SRAM near compute  L1 L2 L3 / shared
DRAM      off-die main memory  DDR or HBM / GDDR

Variables that differ
cores          few fat cores                 many thin cores
control area   large                         small and replicated
ALU count      low                           high
cache / core   large private + big shared    small local + shared
memory links   fewer                         more
goal           low latency                   high throughput
thread model   1 to tens of threads          thousands of threads
execution      MIMD, out of order            SIMT / SIMD lockstep
occupancy      keep one thread fast          hide latency with many threads

Fundamentals
CPU spends die area on control and cache so one thread finishes sooner
GPU spends die area on ALUs and bandwidth so many threads finish together
same DRAM at the bottom, different pressure on it
CPU wants lower latency
GPU wants higher bandwidth

Typical mapping
CPU   OS, compilers, JIT, gameplay logic, OLTP, branchy serial work
GPU   shaders, ML kernels, data-parallel physics, image filters, GEMM
mixed video engines, NPUs, and iGPUs sit beside both
